{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would present a sub-standard quality of internal accommodation of both the flats failing to meet the internal space standards in terms of GIA, built-in storage and&nbsp;the size bedroom 3 in the ground floor flat. Further, the ground floor flat bedroom 3 would feature a small&nbsp;inaccessible skylights thus presenting poor ventilation and access to natural daylight. To further this, the first floor flat would have no access to private external amenity space. The combined impact would result in a sub-standard quality of internal and external accommodation of the flats.&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC , December 2023); Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); Policies CP3 and CC1 of the LDF Core Strategy (July 2010); Policies BP6, BP8 and BP11 of the LDF Borough Wide Development Plan Policies DPD (March 2011); Policies SP2, SP3 and DMD1 of the Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Main Modifications version, December 2021);DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)."
  ],
